From: At30c <PabloAtsoc9993@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 03:50:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: finish doze charging animation on main thread

The One UI 9 charging path enters DOZE_AOD correctly and displays its charging
animation, but its timeout coroutine closes the session from a SystemUIBg
thread. PluginAOD then asks DozeMachine to leave DOZE_AOD from that background
thread, which is rejected by Assert.isMainThread(). The failed callback leaves
the display active after the animation has disappeared.

Post chargingAnimStarted(false) to PluginAODManager's main-looper handler so
DozeMachine can complete the transition. Also avoid the newer force-ON display
override on the Exynos 990 stack; the animation already renders through the
DOZE_AOD path, matching the legacy device behavior.

---
 ...DozeChargingSessionImpl$$ExternalSyntheticLambda0.smali | 33 ++++++++++++++
 .../aod/AodTriggerExecutor$DozeChargingSessionImpl.smali   | 10 ++++-
 .../power/feature/aod/AodTriggerController.smali            |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 43 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

